{"id":1769468,"retrievedAt":"2026-09-13T15:10:12.492Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/5jtJ98kibJAYNoqbSHMO7D1thfQ.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[],"homepage":"","id":1769468,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["JP"],"original_language":"ja","original_title":"THE けやき坂 GUERRiLLA BiSH at ROPPONGi HiLLS ARENA","overview":"On 29 November 2017, the day their second major-label album THE GUERRiLLA BiSH went on general sale, the six members of BiSH - the self-styled “punk band that doesn't play instruments” - went out to ambush Tokyo. Announced only that morning on NTV's breakfast show Sukkiri, the free open-air gig “THE Keyakizaka GUERRiLLA BiSH” pulled roughly 2,000 fans to Roppongi Hills Arena at a few hours' notice. Flanked by bodyguards, the group rolled up in a white stretch Hummer and walked a red carpet laid straight through the crowd before tearing into six songs from the new record: My landscape, SMACK baby SMACK, Promise the Star, FOR HiM, GiANT KiLLERS and BiSH -Hoshi ga Matataku Yoru ni-. “We came to guerrilla Roppongi tonight!” Cent Chihiro Chittiii told the packed plaza, the blue Keyakizaka winter illumination glittering behind the stage. AbemaTV streamed the set live.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/nMymSvkFZ7JYR3kBZUzy74mH46V.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"","revenue":0,"runtime":0,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"BiSH: THE Keyakizaka GUERRiLLA BiSH at Roppongi Hills Arena","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"external_ids":{"imdb_id":null,"wikidata_id":null,"facebook_id":null,"instagram_id":null,"twitter_id":null},"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":1,"id":2284032,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Cent Chihiro Chittiii","original_name":"セントチヒロ・チッチ","popularity":0.4484,"profile_path":"/6ElXLkaBILn8cp0Bbx75lWN0xLT.jpg","cast_id":1,"character":"Herself","credit_id":"6aa628065cbe7e